    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8288",
      "problem": "What is the dimension of $\\mathbb{R}_6[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $6?$",
      "worked_solution": "The standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}_n[t]$ is\n\n$$\n\\{1, \\: t, \\: t^2, \\: \\ldots, \\: t^n\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard basis of $\\mathbb{R}_6[t]$ is \n\n$$\n\\{1, \\: t, \\: t^2, \\: \\ldots, \\: t^6\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim}(\\mathbb{R}_6[t])=6+1=7.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{dim}(\\mathbb{R}_n[t])=n+1.\n$$",
